# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
# Cargo.lock is committed for CI reproducibility (cargo vet requires exact versions)

# Landing-page crates are excluded from the workspace, so they build into their
# own target/ dirs; the site also emits a dist/ via Trunk. Their Cargo.lock is
# committed (they're apps) for reproducible builds.
/crates/site/dist/
/crates/site/dist-snapshot/
/crates/site/target/
/crates/site-e2e/target/
# gh-pages worktree the Pages deploy assembles in CI.
/gh/
# Walkthrough receipts (screenshots + trace) are generated by the dogfood test
# and regenerated by CI on every deploy. Don't commit stale binaries, but keep
# the dir (with .gitkeep) so Trunk's copy-dir works on a fresh checkout.
/crates/site/public/receipts/*
!/crates/site/public/receipts/.gitkeep
# The architecture tree `asbuilt docs` writes for the landing site, same
# arrangement: generated on every deploy, dir kept for Trunk's copy-dir.
/crates/site/public/architecture/*
!/crates/site/public/architecture/.gitkeep

# What `asbuilt render`, `export json` and `docs` write beside the committed
# architecture model. SVGs vary with the Graphviz version, so committing them
# would make every render a diff; model.c4 and views.c4 are the source of
# truth and the diagrams are regenerated on demand.
/docs/architecture/views/
/docs/architecture/site/
/docs/architecture/model.json

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Environment
.env
.env.local

# Documentation

# nextest logs the CI test steps tee so the flaky-test reporter can read
# them back; running those commands locally leaves the same files behind.
/nextest-main.log
/nextest-stress.log

# cargo-mutants
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# Claude Code runtime state
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Project-scope skill installs; .claude/skills/ stays tracked (contributor skills)
/.agents/skills/
